---
# Firebase AI Logic server prompt template (dotprompt format).
# Template ID: template_screen_generate  → Remote Config key: template_screen_generate
# Called from src/ai/hybrid.ts runBigCloudJob() for ui-mode "generate a whole
# screen". The client sends templateVariables { request, preamble }; CODE expands
# and re-validates the returned document into a Frame, so this only shapes the
# model and is never trusted.
model: googleai/gemini-3.5-flash-lite
config:
  temperature: 0.2
  responseMimeType: application/json
input:
  schema:
    request: string
    preamble?: string
  default:
    preamble: ""
output:
  schema:
    preset?: string
    padding?: number
    gap?: number
    align?: string
    clarify?: string
    nodes(array):
      type: string
      role?: string
      text?: string
      label?: string
      fill?: string
      inputType?: string
      direction?: string
---
{{preamble}}
You design ONE whole, believable UI screen as a JSON DOCUMENT (NOT ops). Reply JSON only, no prose:
{"preset":"desktop|mobile","padding":32,"gap":16,"align":"stretch","nodes":[{"type":"text","role":"heading","text":"Welcome back"},{"type":"input","inputType":"email","label":"Email"},{"type":"input","inputType":"password","label":"Password"},{"type":"button","label":"Sign in","fill":"blue"}]}
Rules: "nodes" is REQUIRED and non-empty, laid out top-to-bottom in a column. Node "type" is one of text|button|input|image|rect|stack. A text node has role heading|body and "text". A button has "label" and optional "fill". An input has inputType text|email|password and a "label". A stack has "direction" row|column and "children":[...] (use a row of stacks for pricing cards). Keep it to at most 40 nodes. Pick "preset":"mobile" for phone screens, else "desktop". If unclear, reply {"clarify":"<short question>"}.
Request: "{{request}}"
